The @EmbeddedId approach creates the key as a first-class object:

```java
// ═══ @EmbeddedId approach ═══

// Key class — @Embeddable, Serializable, equals/hashCode
@Embeddable
public record DailyBalanceId(
    @Column(name = "account_id") String accountId,
    @Column(name = "balance_date") LocalDate balanceDate
) implements Serializable {}
// Record auto-generates: equals, hashCode, Serializable — perfect for composite keys!

// Entity uses the key as one field:
@Entity
@Table(name = "daily_balances")
public class DailyBalance {
    @EmbeddedId
    private DailyBalanceId id;  // composite key as one object

    private BigDecimal balance;
    private BigDecimal dayChange;

    // Access key fields: entity.getId().accountId(), entity.getId().balanceDate()
}

// Repository:
public interface DailyBalanceRepository extends JpaRepository<DailyBalance, DailyBalanceId> {
    // findById takes the composite key object:
    Optional<DailyBalance> findById(DailyBalanceId id);
    // Custom query using embedded key fields:
    List<DailyBalance> findByIdAccountId(String accountId);
    // Spring Data navigates: id → accountId
}

// Usage:
DailyBalanceId key = new DailyBalanceId("SAV2001", LocalDate.now());
Optional<DailyBalance> balance = repo.findById(key);
```

The @IdClass approach puts key fields directly on the entity:

```java
// ═══ @IdClass approach ═══

// ID class — plain class/record, Serializable, equals/hashCode
public record DailyBalanceId(String accountId, LocalDate balanceDate) implements Serializable {}

// Entity has MULTIPLE @Id fields that mirror the ID class:
@Entity
@Table(name = "daily_balances")
@IdClass(DailyBalanceId.class)
public class DailyBalance {
    @Id @Column(name = "account_id") private String accountId;   // @Id field 1
    @Id @Column(name = "balance_date") private LocalDate balanceDate;  // @Id field 2

    private BigDecimal balance;
    private BigDecimal dayChange;

    // Access key fields directly: entity.getAccountId(), entity.getBalanceDate()
    // No entity.getId() wrapper!
}

// Repository same:
public interface DailyBalanceRepository extends JpaRepository<DailyBalance, DailyBalanceId> {}

// Usage — same lookup:
DailyBalanceId key = new DailyBalanceId("SAV2001", LocalDate.now());
Optional<DailyBalance> balance = repo.findById(key);
```

When to use which:

```java
// @EmbeddedId:
// + Key is a first-class object — can be passed around, used in maps
// + Cleaner for JPQL: "WHERE d.id.accountId = :accountId"
// + One field on entity — less repetition
// - Access: entity.getId().getAccountId() — extra navigation

// @IdClass:
// + Fields directly on entity — entity.getAccountId() (flatter)
// + Works with legacy schemas where entity already has separate fields
// + Some Spring Data derived queries work more naturally
// - Entity and IdClass have duplicate field declarations

// RECOMMENDATION: @EmbeddedId with Java record — cleanest, least boilerplate
```

